  @.82 text "Category:Standards TrackPublished:June 2022ISSN:2070-1721Authors:R. Fielding, Ed.AdobeM. Nottingham, Ed.FastlyJ. Reschke, Ed.greenbytes"
  @.98 # RFC 9110
  @.99 # HTTP Semantics
  @.100 link "Abstract" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#abstract"
  @.102 text "The Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) is a stateless application-level protocol for distributed, collaborative, hypertext information systems. This document describes the overall architecture of HTTP, establishes common terminology, and defines aspects of the protocol that are shared by all versions. In this definition are core protocol elements, extensibility mechanisms, and the "http" and "https" Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) schemes."
  @.103 text "This document updates RFC 3864 and obsoletes RFCs 2818, 7231, 7232, 7233, 7235, 7538, 7615, 7694, and portions of 7230."
  @.104 link "Status of This Memo" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-status-of-this-memo"
  @.106 text "This is an Internet Standards Track document.This document is a product of the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF). It represents the consensus of the IETF community. It has received public review and has been approved for publication by the Internet Engineering Steering Group (IESG). Further information on Internet Standards is available in Section 2 of RFC 7841.Information about the current status of this document, any errata, and how to provide feedback on it may be obtained at "
  @.109 link "https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9110" url="/info/rfc9110"
  @.111 text "."
  @.112 link "Copyright Notice" url="/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-copyright-notice"
  @.114 text "Copyright (c) 2022 IETF Trust and the persons identified as the document authors. All rights reserved.This document is subject to BCP 78 and the IETF Trust's Legal Provisions Relating to IETF Documents ("
  @.116 link "https://trustee.ietf.org/license-info" url="https://trustee.ietf.org/license-info"
  @.118 text ") in effect on the date of publication of this document. Please review these documents carefully, as they describe your rights and restrictions with respect to this document. Code Components extracted from this document must include Revised BSD License text as described in Section 4.e of the Trust Legal Provisions and are provided without warranty as described in the Revised BSD License.This document may contain material from IETF Docume
